  "fallbacks": [
    "It has one base mode, light, and locks every display mode to it: a white poster has no night. High contrast renders its stored high-contrast-v2 set, and print renders the light set."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Languages whose material reads surface-prominent, such as glass and paper gradients, tint their cards the poster's yellow under this scheme: gated and legible, but loud.",
    "Text on emphasis isn't a gated pair. Black on this red reads 6.4:1, but a sticker can count on that only under this scheme."
  ],
